        "parms": "# + - * / % !- !/ — arithmetic\nEach takes two numbers. The left inlet is hot: a number there is worked out with the stored right operand and sent at once. The right inlet is cold: it only stores the operand for next time. The argument is the starting right operand, 0 by default.\nMax's + also works out again on a bang, and keeps to ints when both operands are ints. Here the left inlet ignores a bang, + - * / !- and !/ always send floats, and % always sends an int.",
